window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-10dd8667120ae18c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"groups-and-provisioning\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">群组与预配</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后附加 <code>.md</code>，即可获得该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>群组用于组织 ChatGPT 工作区中的人员，也可以为群组分配自定义角色。群组成员关系本身不会取代席位分配、授予工作区功能权限、覆盖本地运行时策略，也不会提供对 Platform API 或已连接系统的访问权限。</p> <p>如需了解完整的控制模型，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"compare-membership-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">比较成员关系来源</h2> <p>当一组人员有共同的访问需求时，可以使用群组，例如试点人员、工作区操作人员，或需要使用同一项受支持功能的成员。</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-group-for-a-shared-access-need\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">为共同的访问需求创建群组</h3> <p>工作区所有者和管理员可以创建和管理群组。对于人数较少或临时组成的使用对象，可创建手动管理的群组；如果成员关系应跟随组织目录，则可从身份提供商同步已有群组。如果成员关系应按照基于 SCIM 用户属性的规则确定，则使用动态群组。</p> <p>每个群组只能有一个权威的成员关系来源：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>群组类型</th> <th>成员关系来源</th> <th>适用情况</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>手动管理</td> <td>ChatGPT 工作区管理</td> <td>群组规模较小、属于临时群组，或未通过目录同步进行管理</td> </tr> <tr> <td>身份提供商管理</td> <td>通过 SCIM 连接的身份提供商</td> <td>成员关系应跟随组织目录及其成员移除流程</td> </tr> <tr> <td>动态群组</td> <td>根据 SCIM 用户属性评估的规则</td> <td>成员关系应随部门或地点等属性变化</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>动态群组会根据你在 ChatGPT Admin 中定义的规则，评估 SCIM 用户属性。有关设置步骤和受支持的属性，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-83d4edfaf8cd6445\">动态群组</a>。</p> <p>手动管理的群组与身份提供商管理的群组可以同时存在。对于身份提供商管理的群组，身份提供商是成员关系来源；后续预配更新可能覆盖在工作区一侧所做的更改。有关当前 SCIM 预配行为和设置步骤，以帮助中心的说明为准。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-the-access-boundary\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">了解访问边界</h2> <p>群组成员关系本身不会授予工作区功能权限。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-a-group-to-the-right-permissions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">将群组连接到正确的权限</h3> <p>工作区所有者可以把自定义角色分配给群组；在支持的情况下，也可以直接分配给成员。请检查每一个适用角色：只要任一角色将某项权限明确设为 <strong>Off</strong>，即使另一个角色授予了该权限，也会拒绝该权限。成员的席位类型和产品资格仍然适用。</p> <p>SCIM 负责预配工作区成员关系和群组分配。它不会授予 GitHub、Google Drive、Slack 或其它已连接系统中的权限，也不会取代本地运行时要求或 Platform API 组织访问权限。</p> <p>工作区 RBAC 与本地运行时要求是彼此独立的控制系统。一个群组可能同时与两者相关，但不要根据工作区中的群组顺序，推断托管要求存在匹配规则或优先级规则。有关已有文档说明的交付方式和本地优先级规则，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"use-current-setup-procedures\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用当前的设置流程</h2> <p>工作区管理细节可能会变化。有关当前界面操作步骤、可用性和限制，请使用以下资料：</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266401-managing-members-seat-types-roles-and-access-in-chatgpt-enterprise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理成员、席位类型、角色和访问权限（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9083985-group-permissions-in-gpts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理群组（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM 集成常见问题（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理工作区设置（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <p><a id=\"verify-joiners-movers-and-leavers\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">验证入职、调岗和离职流程</h3> <ul> <li><strong>入职：</strong> 确认成员接受待处理的工作区邀请，并获得预期的席位、群组成员关系、权限和受支持功能。</li> <li><strong>调岗：</strong> 更新权威的成员关系来源，并核实成员在所有适用角色共同作用下的有效权限。</li> <li><strong>离职：</strong> 通过身份提供商移除由 SCIM 管理的成员访问权限，并确认该成员已无法访问工作区。如果只从工作区中移除成员，后续同步可能恢复其访问权限。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c\">用户生命周期管理</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">身份验证</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员上线指南</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"groups-and-provisioning\">Groups and provisioning</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Groups organize people in a ChatGPT workspace and can carry custom roles. Group membership doesn't replace seat assignments, grant workspace feature permissions by itself, override local runtime policy, or provide access to the Platform API or connected systems.</p> <p>For the complete control model, see <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"compare-membership-sources\">Compare membership sources</h2> <p>Use groups for people with a shared access need, such as a pilot cohort, workspace operators, or members who need the same supported feature.</p> <h3 id=\"create-a-group-for-a-shared-access-need\">Create a group for a shared access need</h3> <p>Workspace owners and admins can create and manage groups. Create a manually managed group for a small or temporary audience, or sync an established group from your identity provider when membership should follow your directory. Use a dynamic group when membership should follow rules based on SCIM user attributes.</p> <p>Each group has one authoritative membership source:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Group type</th> <th>Membership source</th> <th>When it applies</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Manually managed</td> <td>ChatGPT workspace administration</td> <td>The group is small, temporary, or not managed through directory sync</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Identity-provider managed</td> <td>Your identity provider through SCIM</td> <td>Membership should follow the organization's directory and member-removal process</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Dynamic</td> <td>Rules evaluated against SCIM user attributes</td> <td>Membership should follow attributes such as department or location</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Dynamic groups evaluate SCIM user attributes against rules you define in ChatGPT Admin. See <a href=\"#/article/a-83d4edfaf8cd6445\">Dynamic groups</a> for setup steps and supported attributes.</p> <p>Manual and identity-provider-managed groups can coexist. For identity-provider-managed groups, the identity provider is the membership source; later provisioning updates can overwrite workspace-side changes. The Help Center owns current SCIM provisioning behavior and setup steps.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-the-access-boundary\">Understand the access boundary</h2> <p>Group membership by itself doesn't grant a workspace feature permission.</p> <h3 id=\"connect-a-group-to-the-right-permissions\">Connect a group to the right permissions</h3> <p>Workspace owners can assign custom roles to groups or, where available, directly to members. Check every applicable role: an explicit <strong>Off</strong> in any role denies that permission, even when another role grants it. A member's seat type and product eligibility still apply.</p> <p>SCIM provisions workspace membership and group assignments. It doesn't grant permissions in GitHub, Google Drive, Slack, or another connected system. It also doesn't replace local runtime requirements or Platform API organization access.</p> <p>Workspace RBAC and local runtime requirements are separate control systems. A group can be relevant to both, but don't infer a managed-requirements matching or precedence rule from workspace group order. Use <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> for the documented delivery and local precedence rules.</p> <h2 id=\"use-current-setup-procedures\">Use current setup procedures</h2> <p>Workspace administration details can change. Use these sources for current UI steps, availability, and limits:</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266401-managing-members-seat-types-roles-and-access-in-chatgpt-enterprise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage members, seat types, roles, and access (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9083985-group-permissions-in-gpts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage groups (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM integration FAQ (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage workspace settings (online)</a></li> </ul> <h3 id=\"verify-joiners-movers-and-leavers\">Verify joiners, movers, and leavers</h3> <ul> <li><strong>Joiners:</strong> Confirm the member accepts any pending workspace invitation and receives the intended seat, group memberships, permissions, and supported features.</li> <li><strong>Movers:</strong> Update the authoritative membership source and verify the member's effective permissions across all applicable roles.</li> <li><strong>Leavers:</strong> Remove a SCIM-managed member's access through the identity provider and confirm that the member can no longer access the workspace. If you remove the member only from the workspace, a later sync can restore access.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c\">User lifecycle management</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Authentication</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> </ul>"};
